From 9d6a32d17f4edee65925297cb5b042f61d49fa5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:33:27 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Refuse a file path with a control byte or invalid UTF-8

A path must be valid UTF-8 with no C0 control byte or DEL.  pathNameAllowed
states the rule, replacing completion.c's nameInsertable, and bufferSetFilename
is how a path becomes a buffer's name.  Four callers: editorOpen, the first
save, C-x C-w and cd.  Saves check before the overwrite prompt; a refusal leaves
the old name.  cd works out every rebased name first and refuses if any fails.

A file with such a name can't be opened from emil; rename it first.  The display
fixes stay: register views also cut long names, and *Tags* isn't covered here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01947MBgCkoERXfoyRGfCmQi
